        "original_id": "407007c6-386f-5cba-bf48-fe99da8b80ed",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Friedrich Ratzel, Rudolf Kjellén\n- Concepts: Lebensraum\n- Organizations: Nazi Party (NSDAP), Nazi Germany\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Friedrich Ratzel was a German geographer and ethnographer who lived from August 30, 1844, to August 9, 1904.\n- Friedrich Ratzel was notable for first using the term Lebensraum in the sense later adopted by the National Socialists.\n- Rudolf Kjellén's work was influenced by Friedrich Ratzel.\n- The Nazi Party (NSDAP) and Nazi Germany supported the most extreme form of the Lebensraum ideology until the end of World War II.",
